WEBVTT

00:00.250 --> 00:03.154
The Advanced trend page is the powerful one.

00:03.274 --> 00:09.634
Instead of a chart somebody else designed, you build
your own — one line per station, per data type,

00:09.754 --> 00:11.962
over any period you like.

00:12.783 --> 00:15.591
Now we're on: Advanced trend.

00:15.711 --> 00:18.783
The most powerful view — a chart builder.

00:18.903 --> 00:24.351
Add one or more data series, choose what each
one plots, and compare stations,

00:24.471 --> 00:27.399
areas and measurements side by side.

00:28.217 --> 00:29.969
Compare more data.

00:30.089 --> 00:36.353
Add another data series (up to 12) to compare
stations or data types side by side.

00:36.473 --> 00:39.881
Each series gets its own colour in the chart
legend.

00:40.683 --> 00:42.291
Pick what to plot.

00:42.411 --> 00:45.267
Every row here is one data series.

00:45.387 --> 00:51.147
Its first choice is where the data comes from:
a single station, or a whole Monitoring Area —

00:51.267 --> 00:55.947
like the built-in Example area — which plots
several stations at once.

00:56.750 --> 00:58.718
Choose a data type.

00:58.838 --> 01:03.806
Only data types this station has actually
recorded are offered, with their unit.

01:03.926 --> 01:06.902
The chart redraws as soon as you change it.

01:07.717 --> 01:09.541
Choose a chart type.

01:09.661 --> 01:13.021
Time series is the classic value-over-time
view.

01:13.141 --> 01:20.005
You can also show this series as a 3D time series, a
heatmap, a scatter plot, or a distribution.

01:20.817 --> 01:23.049
Focus on a time period.

01:23.169 --> 01:26.385
Drag the two handles to narrow the time
window.

01:26.505 --> 01:30.369
It applies to every series and sets the
chart's x-axis.

01:31.183 --> 01:33.415
Open the advanced options.

01:33.535 --> 01:39.703
This little summary shows how a series is
drawn (interval · axis · chart number).

01:39.823 --> 01:45.127
Click it to open the drawer with the advanced
controls — the next two tips look inside.

01:45.950 --> 01:49.286
Draw: style, chart & axis.

01:49.406 --> 01:53.222
Show as switches between line, bar and area.

01:53.342 --> 01:56.990
Chart moves the series onto its own numbered
chart below.

01:57.110 --> 02:02.750
Axis puts it on the left or right scale —
useful when two series use different units.

02:03.583 --> 02:05.911
Transform & normalize.

02:06.031 --> 02:12.847
Interval buckets readings by day, week, month
or year, and Aggregate picks how they combine.

02:12.967 --> 02:16.063
Transform can smooth or clip outliers,

02:16.183 --> 02:23.215
and Normalize rescales values (for example to
0–1) so different units fit on one chart.

02:24.017 --> 02:25.625
Read your chart.

02:25.745 --> 02:27.593
The result draws here.

02:27.713 --> 02:34.313
Drag the small slider under the chart to zoom into a
period, and use the legend to tell the series apart.

02:35.117 --> 02:36.845
Save your view.

02:36.965 --> 02:38.693
Happy with a chart?

02:38.813 --> 02:43.229
Save it as a named view and load it again any
time from this menu.

02:43.349 --> 02:45.797
Set default ★ marks your favourite.

02:46.617 --> 02:48.561
That is the whole page.

02:48.681 --> 02:53.337
You can replay this tutorial any time from the
Learning page inside the app.

02:53.457 --> 02:56.121
Thanks for helping look after our water.
